@lang en
IMPORT `tasco-ch6-additional`

-- Tests for Chapter II (own damage) and the own-damage clauses of Chapter VI. Expected values
-- are worked by hand from the figures the rules print; the working is beside each group.
-- A failing assertion is a finding, never a value to edit.

§ `Tests — own damage`

§§ `Helpers`

-- The amount an answer pays: the settlement's last step, or nothing for a loss not covered.
GIVEN `the answer` IS AN `An own-damage answer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount paid by` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `own damage payable` s       THEN s's `payable`
    WHEN `own damage not covered` r e THEN 0

GIVEN `the answer` IS AN `An own-damage answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`covered:` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `own damage payable` s       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `own damage not covered` r e THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the policy`         IS A `A policy`
      `the circumstances`  IS A `The circumstances`
      `the conduct`        IS A `The conduct after the loss`
      `the determinations` IS A `Tasco's determinations`
      `the loss`           IS AN `An own-damage loss`
      `the facts`          IS A `Facts for the additional clauses`
GIVETH AN `An own-damage answer`
`claim` `the policy` `the circumstances` `the conduct` `the determinations` `the loss` `the facts` MEANS
    `the own-damage answer under` `the policy` `in` `the circumstances` `the conduct` `the determinations` `of` `the loss` `with the clauses, given` `the facts`

GIVEN `the codes` IS A LIST OF `An additional clause`
GIVETH A `A policy`
`the standard policy with` `the codes` MEANS
    `a policy on` `a private car` `, own damage` 600000000 `, accident` 100000000 `, clauses` (map (GIVEN c YIELD `the clause` c) `the codes`)

GIVEN `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A policy`
`a policy from 10 January 2025 to` `the end` MEANS
    `A policy` WITH
        `the vehicle`                      IS `a private car`
        `date of conclusion`               IS YMD 2025 1 10
        `start of the period of insurance` IS YMD 2025 1 10
        `end of the period of insurance`   IS `the end`
        `application signed`               IS TRUE
        `premium paid in full and on time` IS TRUE
        `premium before tax`               IS 12000000
        `own damage`                       IS JUST (`An own-damage section` WITH `sum insured` IS 600000000, `deductible stated on the policy` IS NOTHING)
        `driver and passenger accident`    IS NOTHING
        `goods liability`                  IS NOTHING
        `voluntary third-party liability`  IS NOTHING
        `additional clauses`               IS EMPTY
        `countries named for BS05`         IS EMPTY
        `added equipment listed`           IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `The conduct after the loss`
`no written notice` MEANS `conduct with notice` NOTHING `, moved:` FALSE `, recourse lost:` FALSE

GIVETH A `The conduct after the loss`
`moved without consent, notice in time` MEANS `conduct with notice` (JUST (YMD 2025 6 16)) `, moved:` TRUE `, recourse lost:` FALSE

GIVETH A `The conduct after the loss`
`moved without consent, no notice` MEANS `conduct with notice` NOTHING `, moved:` TRUE `, recourse lost:` FALSE

§§ `Article 15.1.3(c) — every row of the parts table, both columns, both edges`

-- Rows: under 1 year 0/0; 1 to under 3 years 0/10; 3 to under 6 15/20; 6 to under 10 25/30;
-- 10 to under 15 35/40; 15 years and over 50/55 (not for business / for business).
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 0   `months of use, for business:` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 11  `months of use, for business:` TRUE  EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 12  `months of use, for business:` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 35  `months of use, for business:` TRUE  EQUALS 0.10
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 36  `months of use, for business:` FALSE EQUALS 0.15
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 71  `months of use, for business:` TRUE  EQUALS 0.20
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 72  `months of use, for business:` FALSE EQUALS 0.25
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 119 `months of use, for business:` TRUE  EQUALS 0.30
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 120 `months of use, for business:` FALSE EQUALS 0.35
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 179 `months of use, for business:` TRUE  EQUALS 0.40
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 180 `months of use, for business:` FALSE EQUALS 0.50
#ASSERT `the rate in` `Article 15.1.3(c) — the table for parts` `for` 400 `months of use, for business:` TRUE  EQUALS 0.55

§§ `Article 15.1.3(d) — every row of the battery table, and the missing row`

-- Rows: under 1 year 0/10; 1 to under 3 30/50; 3 to under 6 50/70; 6 to under 10 70/80;
-- 10 to under 15 90/90. Nothing for 15 years or more (finding X-11).
