-- An engine damaged while driving through a flooded area: 13.6.
#ASSERT `Article 13 — the exclusions of an item, in` (`a loss by` `a natural catastrophe beyond control` `of` EMPTY `, estimate` 0 `, value before` 780000000 `, theft decided:` FALSE `, flooded:` TRUE) `:` (`an item` `an electrical or electronic part, or an engine` `costing` 50000000 `, replaced:` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `13.6 engine or electrics in a flooded area`
-- A cause Article 11 does not name: 13.1.
#ASSERT `Article 13 — the exclusions of the whole loss for` `a private car` `and` (`a loss by` `a cause Article 11 does not name` `of` `the collision damage` `, estimate` 0 `, value before` 780000000 `, theft decided:` FALSE `, flooded:` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `13.1 outside the cover of Article 11`

§§ `Article 15.2.1 — a total loss, both sides of 75%`

-- Market value before the loss 900 million: 75% is 675 million. 676 million is a total loss;
-- 675 million is not ("trên 75%").
#ASSERT `Article 15.2.1 — the extent of` (`a loss by` `collision, overturning, falling, sinking or impact by an external object` `of` EMPTY `, estimate` 676000000 `, value before` 900000000 `, theft decided:` FALSE `, flooded:` FALSE) EQUALS `a total loss`
#ASSERT `Article 15.2.1 — the extent of` (`a loss by` `collision, overturning, falling, sinking or impact by an external object` `of` EMPTY `, estimate` 675000000 `, value before` 900000000 `, theft decided:` FALSE `, flooded:` FALSE) EQUALS `a partial loss`
-- The whole car stolen: a total loss once the investigation is concluded or suspended; before
-- that, the chapter does not say (finding X-13).
#ASSERT `Article 15.2.1 — the extent of` (`a loss by` `theft or robbery of the whole vehicle` `of` EMPTY `, estimate` 0 `, value before` 700000000 `, theft decided:` TRUE `, flooded:` FALSE) EQUALS `a total loss`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` (`a loss by` `theft or robbery of the whole vehicle` `of` EMPTY `, estimate` 0 `, value before` 700000000 `, theft decided:` FALSE `, flooded:` FALSE) `no clause facts`) BECAUSE "a theft of the whole car is not a total loss until the investigation is concluded or suspended"

§§ `The settlement: cover, depreciation, proportion, costs, reduction, deductible, limit`

-- THE COLLISION on the standard policy (sum insured 600 million on a car worth 800 million, no
-- deductible on the policy, 34 months of use, not a business car):
--   bumper 20,000,000 replaced, rate 0% (1 to under 3 years, not business)   20,000,000
--   headlamp 10,000,000 repaired, not depreciated                            10,000,000
--   tyre 4,000,000 replaced with the other parts, 50% under 15.1.3(e)         2,000,000
--   windscreen 6,000,000 replaced, not depreciated                            6,000,000
--   items allowed                                                            38,000,000
--   x 600/800 for under-insurance (15.1.4(b))                                28,500,000
--   + towing 2,000,000 (at most 10% of 600 million)                          30,500,000
--   no reduction ground; less the deductible of 500,000 (15.1.5)            30,000,000
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 30000000

-- The same with no written notice: 10% off (14.1.1(b)): 30,500,000 x 0.9 - 500,000 = 26,950,000.
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `no written notice` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 26950000

-- An objective obstacle excuses the notice duty of 5.2.7(c) but not the 10% of 14.1.1(b) (X-04).
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `conduct with an objective obstacle and no notice` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 26950000

-- A business car: the bumper at 10%, 18,000,000; items 36,000,000; x 0.75 = 27,000,000; + 2,000,000;
-- less 500,000 = 28,500,000. With BS01 (no depreciation): back to 30,000,000.
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` (`a policy on` `the same car used for business` `, own damage` 600000000 `, accident` 100000000 `, clauses` EMPTY) `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 28500000
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` (`a policy on` `the same car used for business` `, own damage` 600000000 `, accident` 100000000 `, clauses` (LIST `the clause` `BS01 new for old`)) `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 30000000

-- Moving the car without consent puts the loss in the 20-50% band; with no rate decided by Tasco
-- the encoding declines; at 30%: 30,500,000 x 0.7 - 500,000 = 20,850,000. With late notice as
-- well, the higher rate alone applies (14.2.1): still 20,850,000.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `moved without consent, notice in time` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts`) BECAUSE "Tasco has not determined a rate within the band of Article 14.1.2"
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `moved without consent, notice in time` (`Tasco decided` (JUST 0.3) `,` NOTHING `, fault` NOTHING) `the collision` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 20850000
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `moved without consent, no notice` (`Tasco decided` (JUST 0.3) `,` NOTHING `, fault` NOTHING) `the collision` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 20850000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `moved without consent, notice in time` (`Tasco decided` (JUST 0.6) `,` NOTHING `, fault` NOTHING) `the collision` `no clause facts`) BECAUSE "Tasco's chosen rate lies outside the band Article 14 allows"

-- Overload (14.1.4): 7 persons in a 5-seat car is 40% over: 30,500,000 x 0.6 - 500,000 = 17,800,000.
-- 6 persons is 20%, not "trên 20%": no reduction, 30,000,000.
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `circumstances with 7 persons` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 17800000
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `circumstances with 6 persons` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 30000000

-- Speeding (14.1.2(c)): 75 in a 60 zone is 25% over, in the band; 72 is 20%, not "trên 20%".
#ASSERT `Article 14.1 — the reduction grounds met by` `circumstances at 75 in a 60 zone` `good conduct` `a private car` EQUALS LIST `1.2(c) speeding by more than 20% and up to 50%`
#ASSERT null (`Article 14.1 — the reduction grounds met by` `circumstances at 72 in a 60 zone` `good conduct` `a private car`)
-- 90 in a 60 zone is exactly 50%: the band reaches it, but Article 10.11 has already excluded the
-- loss (finding X-09).
#ASSERT NOT `covered:` (`claim` `the standard policy` `circumstances at 90 in a 60 zone` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts`)

-- Exclusions reach the answer: abroad without BS05, premium unpaid, a policy before 15/11/2024.
#ASSERT `claim` `the standard policy` `circumstances abroad in Laos` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts` EQUALS `own damage not covered` (LIST (`Article 10:` `10.1 outside Vietnam`)) EMPTY
#ASSERT `claim` `a policy with the premium unpaid` `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts` EQUALS `own damage not covered` (LIST `Article 2.1: outside the period, or the premium unpaid`) EMPTY
#ASSERT REFUSED `claim` `a policy concluded before the rules took effect` `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts` BECAUSE "a contract concluded before 15 November 2024 is governed by Decision 53/2024, which is not in this encoding"

-- A total loss: market value before the loss 900 million, capped at the 600 million insured;
-- towing 2 million added and then cut back by the ceiling of 11.3; no deductible on the policy.
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` (`a loss by` `collision, overturning, falling, sinking or impact by an external object` `of` EMPTY `, estimate` 700000000 `, value before` 900000000 `, theft decided:` FALSE `, flooded:` FALSE) `no clause facts`) EQUALS 600000000

-- Double insurance (Article 8): 600 million here and 600 million elsewhere on a car worth 800
-- million; Tasco pays 600/1,200 of the 30,000,000: 15,000,000.
GIVETH AN `An own-damage loss`
`the collision, insured elsewhere for 600 million` MEANS
    `An own-damage loss` WITH
        `cause`                                                          IS `collision, overturning, falling, sinking or impact by an external object`
        `sudden and unforeseen`                                          IS TRUE
        `items`                                                          IS `the collision damage`
        `cost of preventing further loss`                                IS 0
        `cost of rescue and towing to the nearest repairer`              IS 2000000
        `market value immediately before the loss`                       IS 780000000
        `estimated cost of repair`                                       IS 40000000
        `investigation concluded or suspended, or prosecution declined`  IS FALSE
        `more than half the paint area damaged`                          IS FALSE
        `cost of repainting the whole vehicle`                           IS 0
        `whole vehicle lost by fraud, breach of trust, civil dispute or unknown cause` IS FALSE
        `wear and tear, inherent vice, loss of value, defect or faulty repair`        IS FALSE
        `vehicle operating in a flooded area`                            IS FALSE
        `caused by the traction battery`                                 IS FALSE
        `caused by incompatible equipment`                               IS FALSE
        `caused by handling outside the manufacturer's standards`        IS FALSE
        `caused by equipment added after manufacture`                    IS FALSE
        `during operation of special equipment`                          IS FALSE
        `caused by a bomb, mine or explosive device`                     IS FALSE
        `repaired in Vietnam`                                            IS TRUE
        `the owner keeps the vehicle`                                    IS FALSE
        `sums insured by other contracts on the same vehicle`            IS 600000000

#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision, insured elsewhere for 600 million` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 15000000

§§ `Chapter VI — clauses that change an own-damage claim`

-- BS03: an engine (50,000,000, repaired) drowned in a flooded area. Without BS03 every item is
-- excluded by 13.6. With it: 50,000,000 x 0.75 + 2,000,000 towing = 39,500,000; deductible the
-- larger of 500,000 and BS03's (10% of 39,500,000 = 3,950,000, at least 3,000,000): 35,550,000.
GIVETH AN `An own-damage loss`
`a flooded engine` MEANS
    `a loss by` `a natural catastrophe beyond control` `of` (LIST `an item` `an electrical or electronic part, or an engine` `costing` 50000000 `, replaced:` FALSE)
        `, estimate` 50000000 `, value before` 780000000 `, theft decided:` FALSE `, flooded:` TRUE

#ASSERT `claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `a flooded engine` `no clause facts` EQUALS `own damage not covered` EMPTY (LIST `every item of the loss is excluded`)
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` (`the standard policy with` (LIST `BS03 water damage to engine and electrics`)) `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `a flooded engine` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 35550000

-- BS04: a stolen mirror (15,000,000, ordinary part, 0%). Lifted while fewer than the allowed
-- thefts have been claimed: 15,000,000 x 0.75 + 2,000,000 = 13,250,000; deductible the larger of
-- 500,000 and (10% = 1,325,000, at least 1,000,000): 11,925,000. Two already claimed on a
-- one-year policy: no more.
GIVETH AN `An own-damage loss`
`a mirror theft` MEANS
    `a loss by` `theft or robbery of a part` `of` (LIST `a stolen mirror`)
        `, estimate` 15000000 `, value before` 780000000 `, theft decided:` FALSE `, flooded:` FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `covered:` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `a mirror theft` `no clause facts`)
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` (`the standard policy with` (LIST `BS04 theft of parts`)) `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `a mirror theft` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 11925000
#ASSERT NOT `covered:` (`claim` (`the standard policy with` (LIST `BS04 theft of parts`)) `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `a mirror theft` (`clause facts with` 2 `thefts claimed,` 0 `days of repair at` 0 `a day,` 0 `days already paid`))

-- BS04's allowance by the length of the contract: under 12 months none (finding X-17), 12 to
-- under 18 months 02, 18 months or more 03. A period ending on 9 January 2026 is a full year.
#ASSERT `BS04 — the part thefts allowed under` (`a policy from 10 January 2025 to` (YMD 2026 1 9)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `BS04 — the part thefts allowed under` (`a policy from 10 January 2025 to` (YMD 2026 1 8)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `BS04 — the part thefts allowed under` (`a policy from 10 January 2025 to` (YMD 2026 7 9)) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `BS04 — the part thefts allowed under` (`a policy from 10 January 2025 to` (YMD 2026 7 8)) EQUALS 2

-- BS05: the collision in Laos, a country named on the policy: covered as at home.
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` (`the standard policy with` (LIST `BS05 own damage outside Vietnam`)) `circumstances abroad in Laos` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 30000000

-- BS06 is not engaged for a car that is not temporarily imported: the proportion stays.
#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` (`the standard policy with` (LIST `BS06 duty-free or temporarily imported vehicle`)) `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 30000000

-- BS08: lifts Article 10.4 for 30 days from the clause's start (10 January 2025): 9 February is
-- day 30, 10 February is day 31.
GIVETH A `Facts for the additional clauses`
`a new car with its factory slip` MEANS
    `Facts for the additional clauses` WITH
        `part thefts already claimed under this contract`                               IS 0
        `licensed to circulate in that country`                                         IS TRUE
        `driver licensed in that country`                                               IS TRUE
        `temporarily imported for re-export, duty-free, or a diplomatic vehicle`        IS FALSE
        `days of repair, from the repair contract to the acceptance record`             IS 0
        `hire cost per day, before VAT`                                                 IS 0
        `days of hire already paid in the period`                                       IS 0
        `new with a factory quality slip, or imported with a quality certificate and customs papers` IS TRUE
        `used only inside a closed site, never on public roads, with chassis and engine numbers`     IS FALSE
        `loss inside the closed site`                                                   IS FALSE
        `a qualifying driving-school vehicle driven by a learner in traffic`            IS FALSE
        `learner not listed, or without card, learner's permit or papers`               IS FALSE
        `instructor without a practising certificate`                                   IS FALSE
        `no learner sign or no auxiliary brake`                                         IS FALSE
        `outside the school's permitted time or route`                                  IS FALSE
        `no instructor beside the learner, outside a test`                              IS FALSE
        `special vehicle not technically safe`                                          IS FALSE
        `operator without the right licence for the special equipment`                  IS FALSE
        `operator deliberately broke the operating instructions`                        IS FALSE
        `a converted or modified goods vehicle`                                         IS FALSE
        `inspection certificate expired at the loss`                                    IS FALSE

#ASSERT `covered:` (`claim` (`the standard policy with` (LIST `BS08 temporary circulation`)) `circumstances on 9 February 2025 with an expired certificate` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `a new car with its factory slip`)
#ASSERT NOT `covered:` (`claim` (`the standard policy with` (LIST `BS08 temporary circulation`)) `circumstances on 10 February 2025 with an expired certificate` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `the collision` `a new car with its factory slip`)

-- BS12 and Article 11.1.5: vandalism in a riot is paid with or without BS12 (finding X-10).
GIVETH AN `An own-damage loss`
`riot damage` MEANS
    `a loss by` `vandalism in a demonstration, riot or public disorder` `of` `the collision damage`
        `, estimate` 40000000 `, value before` 780000000 `, theft decided:` FALSE `, flooded:` FALSE

#ASSERT `the amount paid by` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `riot damage` `no clause facts`) EQUALS 30000000
#ASSERT `BS12 — the clause covers` `riot damage`

-- Item 16: a policy carrying a clause agreed outside the rules, and a loss the rules do not pay
-- (a tyre damaged alone): declined rather than answered "not covered".
GIVETH AN `An own-damage loss`
`a tyre burst` MEANS
    `a loss by` `collision, overturning, falling, sinking or impact by an external object` `of` (LIST `a tyre damaged alone`)
        `, estimate` 4000000 `, value before` 780000000 `, theft decided:` FALSE `, flooded:` FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `covered:` (`claim` `the standard policy` `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `a tyre burst` `no clause facts`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `claim` (`the standard policy with` (LIST `BS16 another clause agreed in writing`)) `clean circumstances` `good conduct` `nothing decided` `a tyre burst` `no clause facts` BECAUSE "the policy carries an additional clause whose terms are not in these rules"

-- BS07: hire at 600,000 a day is paid at 500,000; 10 days of repair less the 04-day deductible is
-- 6 days: 3,000,000. With 28 days already paid in the period, only 2 more: 1,000,000. Three days
-- of repair: nothing.
